  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "If \\(a,\\) \\(b,\\) \\(c,\\) \\(d\\) are positive real numbers such that \\(a,\\) \\(b,\\) \\(c,\\) \\(d\\) form an increasing arithmetic sequence and \\(a,\\) \\(b,\\) \\(d\\) form a geometric sequence, then \\(\\dfrac{a}{d}\\) is",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{12}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{6}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{4}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{3}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": "1/4"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12b-2002-p9.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let \\(b=a+r,\\) \\(c=a+2r,\\) \\(d=a+3r.\\) The geometric condition \\(b^2=ad\\) gives \\((a+r)^2=a(a+3r),\\) i.e. \\(r^2=ar,\\) so \\(r=a.\\)\n\nThen \\(d=a+3a=4a\\) and \\(\\dfrac{a}{d}=\\dfrac14.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Write \\(b=a+r,\\) \\(c=a+2r,\\) \\(d=a+3r\\)",
        "The geometric condition \\(b^2=ad\\) gives \\(r^2=ar,\\) so \\(r=a\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
